\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel's Rise Raises  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expectations In  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Amy Teibel \par \uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1997\par 13:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel's recent strengthening has sparked expectations that the Bank of Israel may have to buy dollars again soon to force the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased more than $6 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  between the beginning of the year and June 18, when it widened the shekel's trading band and ended the immediate need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's immediate response to the wider band was to buy dollars, and the shekel fell 4.9% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  between June 18 and June 30. \par \par \uc2  But recent statistics indicating stronger-than-expected inflationary pressures have bolstered the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by damping expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might cut the discount rate next month from the current 12.7%. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been gaining ground for four consecutive sessions, a dealer in the Tel Aviv trading room of The First International Bank of Israel noted. The dollar traded at about 3.5220 shekels at 1045 GMT, compared with Friday's fixing of 3.5320 shekels and Wednesday's fixing of 3.5560 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also traded at 3.7950 shekels against its basket, compared with Friday's fixing of 3.8066 shekels and Wednesday's fixing of 3.8337 shekels. The shekel is adjusted daily against a basket of major international monies dominated by the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'People don't think the discount rate will go down - either it will stay where it is or it will go up - so they can continue borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' the First International Bank of Israel dealer said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1107GMT \par \par \uc2  1142 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7l05bey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
