\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Strengthens Slightly Vs Dlr In Light Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1997\par 16:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The Israeli shekel rose 0.11% against the dollar Wednesday in light trading. Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers attributed the rise to a published report that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading no matter how sharp the swings. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.569 to the dollar compared with 3.573 to the dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of 3.55 to 3.578 to the dollar, dealers said. Shortly after the 1230 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at 3.55. \par \par \uc2  ``Customers are still pretty uptight,'' said Elad Shraga, a dealer at Israel Discount Bank. The report about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ``put more risk into the market,''he said. \par \par \uc2  Shraga said the bid-to-offer spreads had narrowed following several weeks of wide spreads that began after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed the shekel's trading band on June 18. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixes the shekel daily against a basket of five major\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dominated by the dollar. On Wednesday, the shekel\par rose 0.24% to 3.8701 against the basket compared with Tuesday's close of\par 3.8794.\par     -By Michele Gershberg\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-07-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1415GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par 