\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Israel - June 30. \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, June 30 (Reuter) - These are some of the leading stories in Israeli newspapers on Monday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  HAARETZ \par \par \uc2  - Foreign Minister Levy once again considering resigning. "I do not trust Netanyahu". \par \par \uc2  - Senior Bank of Israel official: Our policy is to let the forces of the market determine the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  - Printing press worker suspected of stealing matriculation Bible exam. \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM POST \par \par \uc2  - Labour legislator Sneh: Arafat ordered enhanced security cooperation. \par \par \uc2  - Levy, prime minster row delays reshuffle. \par \par \uc2  - Netanyahu condemns anti-Islam leaflets. Islamic movement protests Hebron flyers. \par \par \uc2  - Phone competition hits last-minute trouble. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : 1997 budget deficit higher than government's target. \par \par \uc2  - Israel will ask United States to expand free trade pact into Jordan. \par \par \uc2  MAARIV \par \par \uc2  - Defence Minister Mordechai proposes that French troops replace Israeli soldiers in south Lebanon. \par \par \uc2  - Foreign Minister Levy considering resigning. \par \par \uc2  - Police say hundreds of high-school students bought Bible matriculation exam. \par \par \uc2  YEDIOTH AHRONOTH \par \par \uc2  - Cabinet minister Sharon: If I'm not appointed to the inner cabinet, I will refuse to serve as finance minister. \par \par \uc2  - Arafat: Sharon has not called me a "war criminal" recently. \par \par \uc2  GLOBES \par \par \uc2  - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 : We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading as necessary. \par \par \uc2  - The anti-monopoly authority raided Bezeq offices; managers will be questioned over rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  - Supersol in negotiations over sale of chain in Hungary; deal estimated at 20 to 25 million dollars. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6u034gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
