\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  wary of  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1997\par 13:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, June 29 (Reuter) - The director of the Bank of Israel's research department said on Sunday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  preferred not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem a further depreciation in the shekel. \par \par \uc2  "We are following what is happening in the market and now our preference is not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Leo Leiderman told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "First of all we have to see how the exchange rate is behaving and then we have to see how the location of the exchange rate within the band affects the inflation environment," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Not every acceleration of depreciation has to be translated into inflation, especially when we are in a period of economic slowdown and unemployment," Leiderman said. \par \par \uc2  He said the Bank of Israel would continue to focus on achieving the government's 1997 inflation target of seven to 10 percent. "Our estimate is that the inflation environment right now is at about nine percent," Leiderman said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel will recommend next year's target be set at six to nine percent, he added. \par \par \uc2  Leiderman hinted that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides it must take steps to control inflation it would prefer to raise interest rates rather sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to let the market forces set the exchange rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  Leiderman said he believes that calm will return to the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market soon. \par \par \uc2  "Our assessment is that...following a certain learning period we'll see fewer fluctuations than what we have seen in the past week," he said. "But we hope there will still be more fluctuations than what we were used to before the change in the exchange rate regime." \par \par \uc2  The shekel plunged five percent last week after the Israeli cabinet approved exchange rate reform that widened the diagonal band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may trade, creating more room for a depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The reform was followed by an interest rate cut of 1.2 percentage points, bringing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key lending rate to 12.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Leiderman said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was committed to defending the upper and lower limit of the band, though market analysts say they believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  well before the shekel depreciates so far that it reaches the upper band. \par \par \uc2  "It's still too early to judge the exact level the exchange rate will reach within the band and it's not reasonable to draw conclusions on the basis of developments over one particular day or week. What's more, we are also seeing technical adjustments," Leiderman said. \par \par \uc2  Many people had sold dollars in advance of the exchange rate measures on expectations of an appreciation of the shekel. Now they are buying back dollars to close positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said some companies are paying off foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans to cut their losses. High Israeli interest rates over the past two years had led many in the private sector to take foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans. \par \par \uc2  "In our assessment, there are now conditions and potential for a significant drop in short-term capital imports to Israel," Leiderman said, noting domestic interest rates are now well below rates of a year ago and that the trend abroad is towards higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.59 shekels) \par \par \uc2  -Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6t03bzt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
