\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Falls Further 1.9% Vs Dollar In Heavy Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par 10:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel weakened an additional 1.9% to 3.59 to the dollar by mid-morning Thursday, continuing its steady fall since its trading band was widened June 18. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume was heavy, with strong demand for dollars, said Guy Levy, a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  'When you have these high rates, people buy,' said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  But Levy said he expected the shekel to rebound as the day progressed, as it has done on previous days after weakening to as much as 3.60 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel had already lost some 3.1% of its value between June 19, the first full day of trading under the new band, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing on Wednesday. On June 19 the shekel closed at 3.4190 to the dollar; on Wednesday, it was fixed at 3.524 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has weakened 8.4% between its Dec. 31 fixing of 3.2510 to the dollar and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The shekel had been so bloated by high discount rates that the Bank of Israel had been forced to buy billions of dollars this year to weaken it and force it back within its trading band. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The widening of the band last week ended the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's immediate\par need to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading, although there\par has been speculation that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par keep the shekel from depreciating too much.\par    -By Amy Teibel\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0821GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6q04m6i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
