\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  -4:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Need Weighed \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1997\par 19:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'Not much has actually happened,' Sapir said. 'They lowered the interest 1.2 percentage points, and that's not a lot. If they were to have lowered the discount rate without changing the trading band, I don't think there would have been such a panic. I think what's happened is the result of uncertainty over what's happened.' \par \par \uc2  'I think stability will be restored by next week and that the dollar will fall below 3.5 shekels,' Sapir said. \par \par \uc2  Because the interest rate differentials remain appreciable and trading volumes aren't big, the market still hasn't found a direction, so there can be speculative movement in both directions, Bar-Shavit said. \par \par \uc2  Katznelson expects to see a much more volatile market as a result of the changes in the trading band. \par \par \uc2  Over the past three years, the exchange rate has moved from the midpoint of the trading band to the ceiling of the band, and that point had become a reference point for evaluating risks, Katznelson said. \par \par \uc2  'Now that reference line is in question and people are wondering what the new reference line will be,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Bar-Shavit predicted that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point to stop the shekel's slide, even if it depreciates several percentage points further. \par \par \uc2  Katznelson thought the market may stop the slide itself by buying short or taking positions as it has in the past, he said. \par \par \uc2  But if the depreciation is quick and sharp, the Bank of Israel could respond by raising the discount rate, though it's too early to tell whether it will, he said. \par \par \uc2  'I think the Bank of Israel wants the markets to feel the implications of taking risks,' Katznelson said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  credit speculations are what created pressures on the Bank of Israel and on the economy in the first place, and the central banks wants to show that the price can be heavy, he said. \par \par \uc2  But if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides the depreciation could be dangerous, it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the discount rate, he said. \par \par \uc2  'A depreciation of 2% a day is something that can't continue for a long time,' he said. 'The longer it lasts, the longer the inflationary effect is felt.' \par \par \uc2  -By Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1721GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6o04r2j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
