\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel weakens in roller-coaster trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, June 18 (Reuter) - The shekel representative rate was fixed slightly lower against the dollar on Wednesday in very volatile trading following a cabinet decision to widen the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After the government approved foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms, a move that triggered the resignation of Finance Minister Dan Meridor, the Bank of Israel lowered its key lending rate by 1.2 percentage points to an annual 12.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was the first rate cut since February. \par \par \uc2  "During early trading the shekel weakened sharply as the market awaited the rate decision. The dollar was traded in a wide spread of about 3.4200/4800 as the rumour was that the Bank of Israel would lower its key lending rate by three percentage points," said Ilan Zadka at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  Zadka said that after the rate announcement the shekel recovered. \par \par \uc2  Meridor strongly opposed widening the shekel's trading bands, fearing it would lead to a further appreciation of the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hurt exports and cause the economy to slow. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was very volatile today and investors were confused. Volume was relatively low as investors remained on the sidelines trying to figure out what was going on," said Guy Levi at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  Levi said the market was looking for direction. \par \par \uc2  "There are still some missing pieces as for instance who is going to be the next finance minister," he said. Meridor's resignation goes into effect on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The shekel had been allowed to trade in a band of seven percent above or below a diagonal slope designed to devalue it by six percent a year. \par \par \uc2  But high interest rates have buoyed the shekel, forcing the Bank of Israel to buy massive amounts of dollars to prevent the shekel from strengthening beyond its band. \par \par \uc2  Under the new plan the lower band remains the same while the upper band rises to 21 percent. The spread between the top and bottom band, therefore, will be 28 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes it will no longer need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  constantly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But Zadka said he believed that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in trading on Thursday as the shekel might appreciate beyond its trading band. \par \par \uc2  "People do not realize that from an economic point of view Meridor is the main winner. The Bank of Israel had to cut the (interest) rate, and the lower diagonal limit remained unchanged, which will force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to buy dollars if the shekel rises," he said. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.4200 shekels, against 3.4170 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7155 against 3.7074 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 3.0191 shekels per 100 yen compared with 3.0051 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9802 shekels compared with 1.9684 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x233 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6i03yo9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
