\par\par \b \uc2  Benefits Of Israel Shekel Band Change Unclear: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Michele Gershberg \par \uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1997\par 21:09\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel won his battle Wednesday against Finance Minister Dan Meridor for a wider shekel trading band, but analysts aren't convinced the move will help the Israeli economy much. \par \par \uc2  Within a year's time, the shekel will gradually be allowed to fluctuate 15% in either direction from an as-yet undetermined midpoint. \par \par \uc2  Under the abandoned system, the shekel was allowed to fluctuate plus or minus 7% from a midpoint that depreciated 6% annually. \par \par \uc2  Immediately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped the floor by 15%, which it will continue to depreciate at a 6% annual rate. The ceiling was left unchanged, but it will depreciate at a rate of 4% rather than 6% previously. Eventually, that will allow the upper half of the band to widen to 15%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the midpoint unchanged for now and didn't say when it will adjust the midpoint again or by how much. \par \par \uc2  According to Frenkel, in the coming year, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions will also be lifted except those on institutional investors that are also imposed abroad. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel touted the change as a means of reducing Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought billions of dollars in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the beginning of the year to weaken the shekel, which has been bloated by the high discount rate. \par \par \uc2  In conjunction with the widening of the band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Wednesday that the discount rate would be cut to 12.7% from 13.9% effective Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 18-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1909GMT \par \par \uc2  1199 1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt6i008xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
