\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Shekel dispute may bring new cabinet row. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tova Cohen \par \uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, June 17 (Reuter) - Talks on expanding the range in which the Israeli shekel can fluctuate threatened on Tuesday to erupt into a power struggle between Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and Finance Minister Dan Meridor. \par \par \uc2  Meridor opposes an expansion of the bands while interest rates are high, fearing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will appreciate, hurting exports. He has locked horns over the issue with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is pushing for wider bands to allow the market a greater say in setting the rate. Netanyahu has not taken a clear position on the issue, but has set a goal of eventually making the shekel fully convertible in world markets. \par \par \uc2  It will be up to the prime minister to make the final decision if Meridor and Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel cannot resolve their dispute. Some analysts speculate Meridor would resign if Netanyahu backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stand. \par \par \uc2  Netanyahu met the two warring sides on Monday but a marathon all-night meeting failed to resolve the issue, fuelling uncertainty on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the day, buying dollars to prevent the shekel from appreciating beyond its trading band, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Hapoalim said. \par \par \uc2  Political analyst Hanan Crystal said Netanyahu might be using the economic talks to move on a government shake-up. \par \par \uc2  "He has in essence begun the great battle for the whole kitty," Crystal told Israel Radio. \par \par \uc2  Israel's media have speculated that Netanyahu intended to juggle his ministers, moving Ariel Sharon from infrastructure to the finance post. \par \par \uc2  Crystal said such a plan would leave young Likud leaders like Meridor, who might challenge Netanyahu for party leadership, outside the government circle. \par \par \uc2  Netanyahu announced after the all-night meeting that a budget cut and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform, including increasing the amount institutional investors and companies can invest abroad, had been agreed. \par \par \uc2  But talks will continue on Tuesday afternoon in Jerusalem on the main issue outstanding -- the shekel's trading bands. \par \par \uc2  The shekel strengthened in early trading. Turnover was low and spreads were very wide, reflecting the uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  "The market doesn't know what will happen," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Hapoalim said. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel has pushed for expanding the bands, which would give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  some relief from the need to constantly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would find its own equilibrium. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates have buoyed the shekel, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy massive amounts of dollars to prevent the shekel from strengthening beyond its band. \par \par \uc2  But Dan Propper, head of the Manufacturers Association, echoed Meridor's concerns that an appreciating exchange rate would hurt the economy. \par \par \uc2  "If the trading band is expanded, we'll see higher unemployment and I'm not sure from a social perspective we'll be able to deal with this phenomenon," he told Israel Television. \par \par \uc2  The shekel, pegged to a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is allowed to trade in a band of seven percent above or below a diagonal slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by six percent a year. \par \par \uc2  Netanyahu dismissed media speculation that Meridor would quit were the bands widened. \par \par \uc2  When asked by reporters whether Meridor would continue as finance minister, Netanyahu replied: "It is not on the agenda." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6h03wjv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
