\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervening \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Shekel - Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par 16:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a heavy hand Tuesday in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying as much as half a billion dollars in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and bring it back within its trading band, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was agitated by uncertainty over the future of the trading band, and dealers said the trading was dominated almost exclusively by dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar at 3.4170 shekels, a 0.029% rise from Monday's close at 3.4160. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded within a range of 3.3850 shekels to 3.4170 shekels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadily throughout the day, and opted for massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  just prior to the market's close, the dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Tal Vardi, a dealer with Bank Hapoalim, attributed the heavy dollar sales to the expectation that Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel will succeed in widening the shekel's trading band during his meeting Tuesday with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and Finance Minister Dan Meridor. \par \par \uc2  'Many think the band will be opened and the shekel will appreciate,' Vardi said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is fixed daily against a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, weighted at 60%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday, the basket was fixed at 3.7074 shekels, a 0.021% rise from\par Monday's close of 3.7066.\par    -By Michele Gershberg\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-06-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1436GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6h04fag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
