\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel keeps shekel down by buying dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, June 16 (Reuter) - The shekel's representative rate was fixed lower against the dollar and the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a relatively high scale by buying dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The session opened with heavy conversions of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on rumours Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu would announce a widening of the shekel's trading bands. \par \par \uc2  Netanyahu is due to speak this evening at an economic conference in the seaside town of Caesarea. \par \par \uc2  "There are rumours Netanyahu will announce a widening of the bands and further liberalisation of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel, pegged to a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is allowed to trade in a band of seven percent above or below a diagonal slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about six percent a year. \par \par \uc2  "Volume was very high today and we saw heavy conversions despite the fact that the Bank of Israel is expected to lower its key lending rate following the lower-than-expected May CPI," said Zahi Elias of Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  May's consumer price index, released on Sunday, rose 0.5 percent -- well under analysts' expectations of 0.7 to 0.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel is scheduled to announce July interest rates on June 23. The base rate has been unchanged at 13.9 percent since the end of February. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates have buoyed the shekel, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in recent months to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating beyond its trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced again to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a relatively high scale buying almost $150 million," Elias added. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.4160 shekels, against 3.4130 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7066 against 3.7048 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9953 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.9867 on Friday, and against the mark at 1.9715 shekels compared with 1.9748 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Dan Meridor opposes a widening of the band, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supports such a move. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters at Caesarea on Monday, Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel said in response to a question on whether a decision has been taken on widening the band: "That's not an issue we need to decide. We are now talking about a variety of measures, all of which are consistent with increasing the freedom of Israelis and investors to operate in the economy, particularly in the area of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalisation. \par \par \uc2  "In this regard, I believe that the prime minister, the finance minister and myself are getting close to decision". \par \par \uc2  He would not comment on the timetable. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.4130 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x233 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6g042za\par }\page