\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel surges against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, June 9 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel's representative rate was fixed sharply higher against the dollar on Monday after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged in Asia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel rose sharply against the dollar today after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped abroad," said Zahi Elias of Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that Japan's trade surplus will be discussed by the Group of Seven (G7) leading industrial nations next week drove the dollar down more than two yen in Asian trade to 111.80, its weakest since November 25, 1996. \par \par \uc2  Elias said that the decline of the dollar pushed the basket downwards forcing the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was acting on a relatively high scale today buying more than $150 million to support the basket," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, which has been trading at the bottom end of its trading band since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Volume was relatively high today because there will be no trading on Wednesday," Elias said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel will not set a representative rate on Wednesday because of the Jewish holiday of Shavuot. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.4010 shekels, against 3.4150 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7021 against 3.7009 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 3.0224 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.9502 on Friday, and against the mark at 1.9842 shekels compared with 1.9748 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.4020 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x233 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt690493x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
