\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel Strengthens Slightly, Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1997\par 15:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel strengthened slightly against the dollar Monday in moderate-to-heavy trading, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel bought more than $100 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and force it back within its trading band, said dealer Oded Zalstein of Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the shekel at 3.4010 to the dollar, a rise of 0.41% from Friday's close of 3.4150 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's fall against the shekel mirrored its fall on major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after the 1230 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading within a range of 3.397 to 3.400 to the dollar, strengthened by the dollar's weakening on international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, they said. \par \par \uc2  Throughout the day, the shekel traded within a range of 3.3970 to 3.4050 to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is fixed daily against a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, weighted around 60%. \par \par \uc2  Because it has strengthened repeatedly this year beyond the strongest point in its trading band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to buy billions of dollars to weaken the shekel. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been bloated by customers who have been taking advantage of Israel's high discount rate to take out loans in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raise capital abroad and convert the money to shekels. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the basket closed at 3.7021 shekels, up 0.032% from Friday's close of 3.7009 shekels. \par \par \uc2  -By Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1330GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt69048ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
