\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel rises after rate decision. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, May 27 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel's representative rate was fixed higher against the dollar and the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after the Bank of Israel decided to leave unchanged its key lending rate for June, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that it was holding its key lending rate for June unchanged at an annualised 13.9 percent, the level at which it has been since the end of February. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel rose today as investors expected a moderate rate cut of 0.5 percentage point or less. The rate decision led to higher demand for the shekel," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  He added that activity was relatively low and that the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now traded at the lower edge of its trading band. "Despite the fact that the basket was traded at the bottom of the band, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket which has been trading at the bottom end of its trading band for four months. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not set a representative rate on Monday because of the U.S. Memorial Day. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3940 shekels against 3.3980 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6947 shekels against 3.7041 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9169 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.9335 on Friday, and against the mark at 1.9969 shekels compared with 2.0093 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.3930 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5r04w19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
