\par\par \b \uc2  Israel's Netanyahu to decide on  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  reform. \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, May 27 (Reuter) - Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a dispute between the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury to advance a programme of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalisation, government sources said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury disagree on details of the liberalisation, especially with regard to investments by Israeli provident funds abroad. \par \par \uc2  Netanyahu will summon \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Jacob Frenkel and Finance Minister Dan Meridor for a meeting soon to resolve the differences, the sources said. No date has been set for the meeting. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel would like to lift foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls over a number of years until the shekel becomes fully convertible. \par \par \uc2  Among the steps the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recommends: \par \par \uc2  - Allowing provident funds and institutional investors to invest up to five percent of their assets in foreign securities against two percent currently; \par \par \uc2  - Allowing companies to invest in foreign securities with no limitation; currently they may invest 10 percent of their capital or five percent of their turnover; \par \par \uc2  - Allowing Israelis to buy dollars freely from banks and open dollar accounts. \par \par \uc2  Talks on the programme began more than a year ago but were halted two months ago after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rejected the Treasury's proposal to gradually increase the amount provident funds may invest abroad. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury's proposal sought to control fluctuations in the level of foreign investment at individual funds, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said was not viable. \par \par \uc2  -Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5r04vz5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
