\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Strengthens Slightly Against Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1997\par 15:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel strengthened slightly against the dollar in quiet trading Tuesday, due to the dollar's decline against the British pound on world markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $100 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar at 3.4100 shekels, a drop of 0.029% over Monday's close of 3.4110 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded within a range of 3.4070 shekels to 3.4120 shekels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Tal Vardi, deputy manager of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Bank Hapoalim, said the quiet trading reflected months of slow movement on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is fixed daily against a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, weighted around 60%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday, the basket was fixed at 3.6825 shekels, a rise of 0.027%\par from the previous day's fixing at 3.6815 shekels.\par    -By Michele Gershberg\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1345GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5603646\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
