\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel official slams exchange rate regime. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1997\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, May 6 (Reuter) - A top Bank of Israel official said in a paper released on Tuesday the current exchange rate system, featuring a fixed trading band to control shekel movement, hurts the economy. \par \par \uc2  "We are telling anyone who will listen: the present situation whereby the Bank of Israel buys large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the commitment placed on it to maintain the (shekel) trading band, hurts market mechanisms and the economy," David Klein wrote. \par \par \uc2  Klein, director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary division, called for a more flexible exchange rate regime. \par \par \uc2  "Exchange rate regimes are not inscribed in the Ten Commandments...but man-made and must be adapted to changing circumstances." \par \par \uc2  Current exchange rate policy allows the shekel to fluctuate in a trading band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against a basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  said recently it had been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying $5 billion this year to prevent the shekel from appreciating above the trading band. \par \par \uc2  "As long as this (need for such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )...continues, the damage and price the economy will pay will increase and the way out will be more costly," Klein wrote. \par \par \uc2  Klein suggested loosening foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations for Israelis by allowing private individuals to hold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts in local banks. \par \par \uc2  "As for the business sector, it is possible to cancel all remaining remnants of exchange control," he said. "There is no reason the Israeli economy cannot by the end of the decade be like all the developed markets and have a completely convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel and the Treasury have been discussing a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalisation programme but officials said final proposals have been delayed by differences mainly over rules for investment abroad by Israeli financial institutions. - Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-5370502 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt56061ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
