\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  $5 Bln  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  In 1Q To Weaken Shekel , \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1997\par 13:55\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Israel bought $5 billion in the first quarter to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band, the Bank of Israel's research department reported on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it soaked up the excess money primarily by offering interest-bearing deposits to commercial banks and by reducing the amount of money it offered in one-day loans to commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't release the cost of its monetary policy until it closes its balance sheet. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been inflated by a high discount rate - currently 13.9% after seven recent cuts - that encourages investors to take out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans or raise money abroad and convert the money into shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily since the beginning of the year to defend its trading band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.4100 to the dollar on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- By Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 30-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1155GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt4u005tr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
