\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel rises against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, April 30 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel's representative rate was fixed slightly higher against the dollar on Wednesday in quiet trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "On Tuesday the shekel started rising against the dollar after the setting of the representative rate as the dollar weakened abroad," said Ilan Zadka at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  "On Wednesday trading was quiet and the shekel was stable, but the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market, buying dollars to support the basket," Zadka said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $70 million to $100 million. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for three months. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.4070 shekels against 3.4100 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6788 shekels against 3.6785 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.6877 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.6918 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9726 shekels compared with 1.9690 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.4060 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4u06759\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip