\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel hits new low against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, April 8 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel's representative rate was fixed at a new low against the dollar on Tuesday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued rising on overseas markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel continued to decline against the dollar as the dollar rose abroad. Overall, trading was very quiet today and the dollar moved in a narrow range of 3.3860 to 3.3890," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  "The basket traded slightly under the lower edge of the trading band and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, buying dollars on a relatively low scale. I believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million to $100 million," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for two months. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3890 shekels against 3.3810 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6656 shekels against 3.6651 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.6848 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.6982 on Monday, and against the mark at 1.9772 shekels after 1.9856 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.3880 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \