\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  Shekel -2: Slight  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1997\par 16:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Toward the end of the day, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated $3 million to $10 million to weaken the shekel and bring it back within its trading band, the FIBI dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket closed at 3.6651 shekels, up 0.04% from Friday's close of 3.6636 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily and almost daily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading since the beginning of the year to weaken the shekel. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been bloated by a discount rate that is so high relative to those for other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that customers often borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raise capital abroad, and convert the money to shekels. \par \par \uc2  The April discount rate is 13.9%, unchanged from March. \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1419GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4702cbu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
