\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Slightly To Weaken Shekel \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1997\par 18:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of Israel bought small amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed Thursday at 3.358 shekels to the dollar, barely off Wednesday's close of 3.3570. \par \par \uc2  The basket of five major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted closed Thursday at 3.6631 shekels, up 0.016% from Wednesday's close of 3.6625 shekels. \par \par \uc2  Market volume was light, and the dollar traded within a narrow range of 3.3560 shekels to 3.3605 shekels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was light because dollar sales fell off sharply from previous days, when companies were converting large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels to pay April 1 salaries, said dealer Isaac Elias of Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  Elias estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $10 million to $15 million; on Tuesday and Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a total of more than $400 million, dealers estimated. \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1655GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4302ehv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
