\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel pays price for inflation stance. \b0\par\par\uc2  By David Rosenberg \par \uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1997\par 14:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, April 3 (Reuter) - The Bank of Israel is paying a heavy price in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in its battle to contain inflation, but the market is convinced the bank will not back down, dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The bank is soaking up dollars flooding into the economy as Israelis increasingly borrow overseas to take advantage of lower comparative interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The foreign loans are prompted by high domestic interest rates imposed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight inflation and offset excess government spending. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to offset massive demand for shekels. On Wednesday alone, dealers said, it bought more than $200 million. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Israel can continue, but it can't go on forever," said Ilan Raviv, manager of Israel Discount Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing. "The amounts aren't sustainable from the shekel point of view. You can't keep printing money." \par \par \uc2  But, he and other dealers said, the market thinks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue on its path for the foreseeable future. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't frighten people because the Bank of Israel governor says if he had to choose between (defending) the exchange rate and inflation, he'd choose (fighting) inflation," said Raviv. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at supporting the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket rate, to which the shekel is officially linked. The rate trades in a band seven percent above or below its midpoint. \par \par \uc2  However since mid-January, the rate has been scraping along at the bottom of the band, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent it from falling through the bottom. \par \par \uc2  The demand for shekels is due to a renewed surge of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing by the Israeli business sector to take advantage of lower foreign interest rates, said Michal Rotlevy, a dealer United Mizrahi Bank. Israel's prime rate is currently 15.4 percent in nominal terms. \par \par \uc2  Borrowers are converting the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels creating huge demand for the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  soaks up the shekels through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and by luring deposits from the commercial banks with high interest rates. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, media reports said the pressure was due to a big \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan Israel Corp took to finance its 667 million shekel purchase of an Israel Chemicals Ltd stake. "We see a lot of big deals in the economy being financed by \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans," said Raviv. \par \par \uc2  Rotlevy said the demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans began at the end of last year, when the market concluded that the Treasury's 1997 budget cuts were insufficient to prompt the Bank of Israel to lower interest rates significantly. \par \par \uc2  She added that the recent acceleration of inflation has strengthened that view. "Everyone is expecting high (consumer price index figures) so the Bank of Israel won't lower interest rates," she said. \par \par \uc2  Borrowers reason that without a cut, the interest rate differential between Israel and abroad will remain wide and the prospects for a significant depreciation of the shekel will be slim. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel has not yet published figures on the extent of capital imports in the first quarter and it will not comment on the extent of its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said is a rough indicator for both figures, have risen $3.8 billion this year to record $15.3 billion at the end of March. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Bank of Israel wants to resolve the problem without having to make concessions on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Israel wants to move towards full \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalisation and stop all \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Rotlevy. \par \par \uc2  Governor Jacob Frenkel reiterated his call for liberalisation earlier this week, but the Treasury is reportedly blocking any such move in hopes of jawboning the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into lowering interest rates. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, the market is betting an an interim move to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, which would alleviate the pressure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Rotlevy. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  may widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by seven, 10 or even 12 percent -- this is the market's reasonable expectation," she said. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.36 shekels) \par \par \uc2  - Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4307tu0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
