\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Heavily To Weaken Shekel \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 1997\par 17:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)-- The Bank of Israel bought exceptionally large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to weaken the shekel against the dollar and return it to within its trading band, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel strengthened slightly against the dollar, which weakened on world markets, dealers said. The Bank of Israel fixed the dollar at 3.3570 shekels, down 0.119% from the March 27 close of 3.3610 shekels. \par \par \uc2  Market volume was heavy, and the dollar traded within a range of 3.3530 shekels to 3.3570 shekels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixes the shekel against a basket of five major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the basket closed at 3.6617 shekels, up 0.081% from 3.6587 shekels on March 27. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought as much as $220 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two dealers estimated. \par \par \uc2  Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was necessary to offset heavy dollar sales, said Ilan Zadka, a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales were heavy because overseas banks were closed for the Good Friday and Easter holidays, and because Israeli companies were converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels to pay April salaries, said \par \par \uc2  'The banks simply accumulated a lot of dollars in the past few days,' Zadka said. 'The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an aggressive way.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily and almost daily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading since the beginning of the year. On Sunday, finance ministry accountant-general Shy Talmon said the Bank of Israel has bought more than 12 billion shekels over the past three months. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1526GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4102b2v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
