\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel slightly higher against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, March 19 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel's representative rate was fixed slightly higher against the dollar on Wednesday in trendless trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market continues to be very quiet with the shekel trading in a narrow range. Despite that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (by buying dollars) on a moderate scale to support the basket," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to defend the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket rate, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for two months. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3650 shekels against 3.3670 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6541 shekels against 3.6536 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7323 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.7405 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9986 shekels after 1.9967 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.3630 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3j08hd4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
