\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  Shekel Closes Dn Vs Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 16:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday to weaken the shekel, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not a heavy as on Monday, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed at 3.3670 to the dollar, down 0.3% from 3.660 Monday. \par \par \uc2  The shekel also weakened against the basket of five major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which it is adjusted. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket was fixed at 3.6536 shekels, up 0.019% from 3.6529 shekels at Monday's fixing. \par \par \uc2  Volume was moderate, and the dollar traded within a range of 3.3640 shekels to 3.3700 shekels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading since early January to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, dealers estimated the Bank of Israel bought as much as $200 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday, they estimated the bank bought about $70 million to $100 million worth. \par \par \uc2  'The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  much less heavily than yesterday,' said Michal Rotlevy, a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been bloated by a discount rate that is so high relative to those for other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - 13.9% after seven recent cuts - that customers borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raise capital abroad and convert the money to shekels. \par \par \uc2  Udi Sella, a dealer at Israel Discount Bank, said that while trading on Tuesday was quieter than on Monday, 'the business sector is still converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels.' \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1550GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3i01x1z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
