\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Closes Stronger Vs Dollar on Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 18:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel closed stronger against the dollar in dull trading on Thursday. The weaker dollar reflected mostly developments in international markets, a trend that has been in effect for the past weeks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 3.3650 shekels, down 0.24%, from Wednesday closing of 3.3730 shekels. Traders said the dollar ranged from 3.3640 shekels to 3.3670 shekels throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel from closing outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. But when compared with previous days, when the Bank had spent between the equivalent of $70 million to $100 million, today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been minimal, said Nahum Edelstein, a trader with Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. The basket closed at 3.6507 against the shekel, up 0.08%, from Wednesday's closing of 3.6504 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in trading for the past weeks to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. \par \par \uc2  There were expectations that there would be larger selling orders of dollars, but this did not materialize said a trader with Israel Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  Usually, the private sectors converts dollars into shekels on the eve of monthly tax payments. \par \par \uc2  -Avi Temkin \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1729GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3d01t39\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
