\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Drops 0.15% Vs Dollar on Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 18:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel closed slightly weaker against the dollar in very quiet trading on Wednesday. The weaker dollar reflected mostly developments in international markets, a trend that has been in effect for the past weeks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 3.3730 shekels, up 0.15% from Tuesday's closing of 3.3680 shekels. The dollar ranged from 3.3690 shekels to 3.3730 shekels throughout the day, traders said. They added that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel from closing outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. The bank spent the equivalent of $70 million to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market has been locked in the same trend for weeks with no change in sight. Trade was dull, with the Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  close to fixing time, said Isaac Elias, a trader with Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. The basket closed at 3.6504 against the shekel, up 0.03% from Tuesday's closing of 3.6502 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in trading for the past weeks to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There are very few surprises in the market. Each day is very similar\par to the previous one. The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the dollar is\par fixed at its daily highs against the shekel, said Allen Langner, a\par trader with Eurotrust Ltd.\par    -Avi Temkin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1710GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3c01tf0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
