\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Stable In Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 18:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel closed nearly unchanged against the dollar in quiet trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Mostly in reflection of international market developments, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthed slightly against the dollar, reinforcing the trend of recent weeks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 3.3680 shekels, down 0.06% from Monday's closing of 3.37 shekels. The dollar ranged from 3.3640 shekels to 3.3690 shekels throughout the day, traders said, adding that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel from closing outside its trading band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent the equivalent of $50 million in purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There were fewer selling orders Tuesday than on Monday, and the Bank of Israel felt less pressure to buy, said Guy Leshem, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. The basket closed at 3.6502 shekels Tuesday, compared with Monday's close of 3.6491 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in trading for the past weeks to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. \par \par \uc2  'Trade was very dull, but maybe there will be increased pressure closer to the weekend, when monthly tax payments have to be made by the private sector, encouraging it to sell dollars,' said a trader with the First International Bank of Israel. \par \par \uc2  -Avi Temkin \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1724GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3b01qhj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
