\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Weakens 0.09% In Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 17:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel weakened against the dollar in very quiet trading on Thursday. The drop mostly reflected developments in international markets, a tend that has been in effect for the past weeks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 3.370 shekels, up 0.09% from Wednesday's closing of 3.3670. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ranged from 3.3670 shekels to 3.37 shekels throughout the day, traders said. They added that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel from trading outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  The bank spent the equivalent of $50 million to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ``The private sector is selling less dollars than in previous days. Nevertheless we do not see a change in the trend in sight,' said Guy Levy, a senior trader with Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. The shekel closed at 3.6467 against the basket, down 0.02% from Tuesday's closing of 3.6466 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading for the past weeks to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. Since the beginning of the year the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent the equivalent of over $2 billion to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1609GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3601nb9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
