\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Weakens in Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 17:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel weakened against the dollar in quiet trading on Monday. The devaluation of the shekel reflected mostly developments in international markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 3.3530 shekls, up 0.15% from Thursday's closing of 3.3480. There was no trading in Friday due to banks being on strike. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ranged from 3.3480 shekels to 3.3540 shekels throughout the day, traders said. They added that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily during the day to prevent the shekel from trading outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  The bank spent about $200 million to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Allen Langner, a trader with Eurotrust Ltd.. He added that there were large selling orders but the rate of exchange remained stable due to the Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. The shekel closed at 3.645 against the basket, a devaluation of 0.07% from Thursday's closising of 3.642 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading this month to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was very similar to the trend of the past weeks, with selling\par orders forcing the Bank of Israel to purchase dollars, said a trader\par with Bank Discount. So far this is a 'no-news market', traders said.\par    -Avi Temkin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1613GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3301hke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
