\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  Shekel Closed Lower As Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervened \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 1997\par 16:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel weakened against the dollar in quiet trade Thursday, with the depreciation mostly reflecting developments in international markets. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed at 3.3480 shekels per dollar, down 0.2% from Wednesday's close of 3.3410 shekels per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ranged from 3.3430 shekels to 3.350 shekels throughout the day, traders said. They added that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at closing time to prevent the shekel from trading outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  The bank spent about $140 million to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  million to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Yael Geltman, a trader with Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  Geltman added that normally there are selling orders at the end of the month. Nevertheless, trade was generally quiet with no exceptional developments. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading this month to keep the shekel from strengthening beyond its strongest point within the trading band. \par \par \uc2  Trading was very similar to the trend of the past weeks, with selling orders forcing the Bank of Israel to purchase dollars, said Nachum Edelstein, a trader with Bank Hapoalim. Until there is a significant cut in discount rate, the present trend is not going to change, he added. \par \par \uc2  Avi Temkin \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1505GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2r01chd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
