\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel drops sharply against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 27 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed sharply lower against the dollar on Thursday in very active trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We haven't seen such a heavy trading in a long time. Volume was high and the dollar rose sharply following its rise abroad," said Ilan Zadka at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The rise of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the basket from falling on the scale of more than $200 million," Zadka said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket rate, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for more than a month. \par \par \uc2  "Activity was boosted by the business sector, which converted foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels for end-of-the-month payments. Volume was also high because the banks will remain closed tomorrow," Zadka added. \par \par \uc2  Israeli bank employees are due to strike tomorrow for the third Friday in a row demanding a five-day work week. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3480 shekels against 3.3380 on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6424 shekels against 3.6418 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7661 shekels per 100 yen against 2.7590 on Wednesday and against the mark at 1.9818 shekels against 1.9947 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.3470 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt2r09cad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
