\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel stable against dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 26 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed almost unchanged against the dollar and the basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday in lacklustre trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was very quiet today and volume was relatively low. The shekel was traded in a tight range. The basket was also stable and the Bank of Israel was not seen in the market," said a dealer at \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket rate, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for more than a month. \par \par \uc2  "The local market is waiting to see what the reaction will be to Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony before the U.S. Congress (later) on Wednesday," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3380 shekels against 3.3390 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6418 shekels against 3.6411 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7590 shekels per 100 yen against 2.7412 on Tuesday and against the mark at 1.9947 shekels against 1.9939 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.3380 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt2q09iwk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\p