\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervened \highlight\uc2 -2: Bought  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Close To $200M \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1997\par 16:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Most trading was interbank and the corporate sector was quiet, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The expiry of options on the dollar on the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange caused options writers to sell large amounts of dollars, said Ilan Zadka, a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  To prevent these huge sales from strengthening the shekel beyond its trading band, the Bank of Israel had to buy close to $200 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Zadka said. \par \par \uc2  Dealer Oded Waldstein of Bank Hapoalim said it was one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heaviest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since the shekel began strengthening beyond its trading band early last month. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading since then. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement that the discount rate would drop three-tenths of a percentage point next month to 13.9% from 14.2% didn't affect the market, said a dealer at First International Bank of Israel. \par \par \uc2  The relatively high discount rate has strengthened the shekel as investors borrow in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and shift the money into shekels to take advantage of the large interest rate differential. \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1532GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par