\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel gains on dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 25 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed higher against the dollar on Tuesday following the decline of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on overseas markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The lowering of the interest rate had no impact on trading today. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, buying dollars to support the basket," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel said on Monday, after the represenative rate had been set for the day, that it was lowering its key lending rate for March by 0.3 percentage point to an annualised 13.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel rose slightly against the dollar because the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined on Monday after the rate was set," said the Hapoalim dealer. "In the near term the basket will remain under pressure because the business sector is continuing to take foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked loans." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket rate, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for more than a month. Traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought over $100 million on Tuesday to support it. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate in a band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3390 shekels against 3.3420 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6411 shekels against 3.6407 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7412 shekels per 100 yen against 2.7332 on Monday and against the mark at 1.9939 shekels against 1.9444 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.3390 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt2p09gvb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
