\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel rises against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 24 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed higher against the dollar on Monday following the decline of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading continues to be influenced by the movements of the dollar abroad. The shekel rose today following the decline of the dollar against the mark," said Zahi Elias of Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market but on a relatively small scale buying more than $70 million," Elias said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket rate, which has been trading at the bottom end of its band for more than a month. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate in a band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market did not react to expectations that the Bank of Israel would cut its key interest rate. If it does reduce the rate it might have some impact on trading later today," Elias added. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel was scheduled to announce its key lending rate for March at 1430 GMT today. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would either leave the base rate unchanged or cut it up to 0.3 percentage point from the current 14.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3420 shekels against 3.3510 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6407 shekels against 3.6386 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7332 shekels per 100 yen against 2.7115 on Friday and against the mark at 1.9944 shekels against 1.9851 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.3405 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2o000us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
