\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Up Slightly Against Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1997\par 16:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)-- The shekel strengthened slightly against the dollar on Thursday after the dollar weakened against major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worldwide, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the dollar at 3.3510 shekels, a drop of 0.030% from Wednesday's close of 3.3520 shekels. \par \par \uc2  Dealers described trading as quiet and said volume was moderate. \par \par \uc2  'What's happening reflects what's happening around the world,' said Norbert Brinker, president of Gift Ltd., a portfolio management company. 'The dollar weakened worldwide and it weakened against the shekel.' \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar traded within a range of 3.3440 shekels to 3.3530 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is adjusted against a basket of five major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar. In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought more than $2.4 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and force it back within its trading band, according to a media report published this week. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. Aviad Bar-Sella, a dealer at \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Discount Bank, described the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as 'moderate.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket was valued at 3.6386 shekels, a rise of 0.005% compared to Wednesday's close of 3.6384 shekels. \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1507GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2k018b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
