\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel declines against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 18 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed lower against the dollar on Tuesday following the rise of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on overseas markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The rise of the dollar in Europe pushed the basket downward and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market buying dollars," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  "Overall volume was low and the Bank of Israel bought dollars on a relatively small scale," he said. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $50 million. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate in a trading band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.3590 shekels against 3.3510 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6378 shekels against 3.6368 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7042 shekels per 100 yen against 2.6983 on Monday and against the mark at 1.9734 shekels against 1.9776 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.3580 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2i009y7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picsca