\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Weakens; Bank Of Israel Buys Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1997\par 17:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel weakened to another record low against the dollar on Wednesday as the dollar strengthened against the German mark and Japanese yen worldwide. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers described trading as nervous and said selling of dollars was heavy. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the dollar at 3.3420 shekels, up 0.33% compared to Tuesday's close of 3.3310 shekels. \par \par \uc2  'The market was very skittish,' said Yael Altman, a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. 'It started with a steep rise of the dollar, but after Bundesbank officials said they don't want the dollar to be so high (against the German mark), the dollar plunged worldwide, and that also brought the dollar down here.' \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded as high as 3.3440 shekels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'It was a very active day,' said Tal Zindorf, an economist at Bank Hapoalim. 'If the dollar continues to strengthen against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket, then the dollar will continue to strengthen against the shekel.' \par \par \uc2  The shekel is adjusted against a basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar. The strengthening of the dollar worldwide weakened the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket against the shekel. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the shekel stregnthened beyond its strongest point in the trading band. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Wednesday, as it has regularly over the past month, to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more than $100 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to force the shekel back within the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket was valued at 3.6337 shekels at the Bank of Israel fixing, up 0.016% against Tuesday's close of 3.6331 shekels. \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1618GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2c015jz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
